WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.490
Considering how much is packed into every
episode of Game of Thrones, it might come

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.860
as a surprise that there are plenty of scenes
filmed for the show that never make it to

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:09.860
air.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:14.770
Luckily, HBO has included many of these deleted
scenes as bonus features for their home releases.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:19.310
And some of these scenes provide important
character details, and even hints at future

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.310
events.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.829
Here's a look at the most important deleted
scenes from Game of Thrones.

00:00:23.829 --> 00:00:26.230
Loras and Margaery - Season 2

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:30.880
In this deleted scene from season two, Loras
and Margaery comfort each other following

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.719
the murder of Renly Baratheon at the hands
of Stannis Baratheon and Melisandre's shadow

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:36.719
assassin.

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:40.600
Loras is clearly more grief-stricken than
his sister, which makes sense, given Renly

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.120
was his true love.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.830
More importantly, viewers get an early glimpse
into Margaery's always scheming mind, as she

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:51.739
carefully steers Loras away from grief and
towards a more pragmatic future supporting

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:53.329
her next political move.

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:58.100
"He was a good man, he was a kind sweet man.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.199
But he is gone now, he doesn't need you anymore.

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:04.530
I need you, our family needs you."

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.790
Doreah and Irri - Season 2

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:11.180
During the second season of Game of Thrones,
Daenerys learned an important lesson in trust

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:17.090
when her handmaiden Doreah betrayed her, murdering
the Khaleesi's confidant Irri in the process.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.570
Fans didn't actually see any of that happen,
but the sequence was actually filmed before

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:22.850
being cut later.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.890
In an interview after her departure from Game
of Thrones, actress Amrita Acharia, who played

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:32.450
Irri, revealed that that she was trying so
hard to make the strangulation scene realistic

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.940
that she actually suffered real injuries to
her neck while filming.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.530
"I had massive bruises on my neck the next
day.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.530
I was proud.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:40.530
Battle scars.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.590
Death scenes are fun."

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.969
Sansa, The Hound, and Tyrion - Season 2

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:49.969
Sandor Clegane has had one of the most dramatic
character arcs of anyone on the show, as the

00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:51.820
Hound has slowly embraced his humanity.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:56.380
That journey began with his relationship with
the imprisoned Sansa in season two.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.810
But it was a rocky beginning, as this deleted
scene shows.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.560
"Would you sing a song for me little bird.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.119
A song about knights and fair maidens.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.620
Come on sing."

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.900
"You won't hurt me"

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:14.300
The scene ends with Tyrion intervening on
behalf of his future wife, giving this brief

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.489
deleted sequence yet another layer of foreshadowing.

00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:20.400
Pycelle and Tywin - Season 3

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.060
Although the audience suspects that Pycelle
is playing his own long game, the other residents

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.959
of King's Landing never quite seem to realize
the grand Maester isn't nearly as feeble as

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:30.959
he pretends to be.

00:02:30.959 --> 00:02:35.180
But in this deleted scene, we discover that
Tywin has known all along.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:39.260
More shockingly, Pycelle reveals that it was
his treachery that allowed the Lannisters

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.670
to conquer the Seven Kingdoms in the first
place.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:47.480
"Since the time I convinced the mad king to
open his gates to you, I have served the interests

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.610
of the house of Lannister, unfailingly."

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:54.400
Given how much goes on in this short scene,
it's a bit surprising they left it on the

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.890
cutting room floor.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.420
Bronn and Shae - Season 4

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:03.290
After Tyrion ends his relationship with Shae
in season four, he sends her away to Pentos

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.980
where he hopes she will be safe.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.519
Later, she shockingly resurfaces to testify
against him at his trial.

00:03:09.519 --> 00:03:10.519
Why?

00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:14.780
Well, the seeds for that were actually planted
in a deleted scene where Tyrion's buddy Bronn

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:19.599
delivers the bad news, along with a speech
about how rich people are all total jerks.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:22.769
You can almost see Shae's love twisting to
spite as he talks.

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:25.390
"These people, even the good ones.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:30.910
They use us as they please and when we are
no longer any use they spit us out and find

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:31.910
someones else they like."

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.340
Good job, Bronn!

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:36.030
Grey Worm and Missandei - Season 5

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:40.360
In this deleted sequence from season five,
we get to see an extended version of a scene

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:44.960
between Missandei and Grey Worm after the
Unsullied named White Rat was killed in a

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.230
Meereen brothel.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:50.470
We get to see a hint of the beginning of the
romance between Grey Worm and Missandei, as

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:55.090
she tells him that she is afraid what might
happen to him if the Sons of the Harpy attack.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.520
"You will be careful."

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.520
"Careful."

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.760
"You will protect yourself."

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.329
"I protect Daenerys Stormborn."

00:04:05.329 --> 00:04:10.320
Of course, shortly after this, Grey Worm was
nearly killed, only surviving thanks to the

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.290
sacrifice of Ser Barristan.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:14.090
Next time, listen to your girlfriend!

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.940
Arya and the Mummers - Season 6

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:21.690
In several parts of season six, Arya works
with the troupe of mummers in Braavos as they

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:26.050
perform their satire of Westerosi current
events, The Bloody Hand.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:30.400
But not everyone in the audience enjoys the
performances as much as Arya, as shown in

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.740
this deleted scene.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.560
"Violence and profanity, how original."

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.860
"Why don't you just leave then."

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:41.480
If you're familiar with the controversy surrounding
the show after the events following Sansa's

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:46.320
wedding to Ramsay Snow in season five, it's
not hard to recognize this deleted scene as

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.410
a subtle dig at viewers who complain about
the show but continue to tune in anyway.

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:53.120
"I'm going on a wild boar hunt."

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:58.380
Thanks for watching!

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:01.410
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:06.760
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

